          "internal/core/config/subsystem.go",
          "internal/core/config/subsystem_test.go"
        ],
        "entry_type": "decision",
        "text": "Alphabetical mapping in `AssignSubsystem`: The config uses overlapping globs for subsystems (e.g. `internal/harness/antigravity/hooks*.go` vs `internal/harness/**`). Since `Subsystems` is a `map[string]SubsystemConfig`, iteration order is random in Go, causing flaky subsystem assignments. I chose to sort the map keys alphabetically before iterating, which made matching deterministic."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "seed-1469d423",
      "dossier_scope": "core/config",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-04T13:49:55+01:00",
      "source": "seed",
      "fields": {
        "anchors": [
          "internal/core/config/config.go",
          ".memory/config.yaml",
          "internal/core/config/config_test.go",
          "ota.Purpose",
          "ota.Description",
          "internal/core/config/subsystem.go",
          "internal/core/config/subsystem_test.go"
        ],
        "entry_type": "decision",
        "text": "Custom `**` matching: Go's `filepath.Match` does not correctly handle `**` for deep recursive directory matching. I added a simple fallback in `AssignSubsystem` to check `strings.HasPrefix` when the glob ends with `/**` to ensure files in deep subdirectories are matched correctly."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "entry_id": "seed-e67606f4",
      "dossier_scope": "core/config",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-04T13:49:55+01:00",
      "source": "seed",
      "fields": {
